From 41a1542e87eb116fad6d78c9d5d036731ba51ff9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Linux-duo <duo@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:16:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/54] Surface Duo: port the remaining linuxduobench patches
 to v7.3

Patches of the v6.19 series that did not apply to v7.3.5:
- already upstream in v7.3 (dropped): 0012-0020 (WCN39xx pwrseq, BT and DT),
  0023/0024 (ath10k skip host-cap quirk), 0025 (smbx charge disable),
  0074-0086 (drm/msm VM + recovery fixes), 0088 (dispcc-sm8250 parent PLL)
- ported by hand: 0028/0029/0031/0034 (qcom_smbx SMB5, driver taken from the series),
  0035 (DSI DSC slices: upstream has the flag, only NO_CMD_BURST kept),
  0038 (dp snapshot guard), 0042 (venus SM8150), 0043 (camss SM8150),
  0051 (wcd934x: keep upstream micbias parsing), 0055 (q6asm close on re-prepare),
  0062 (IPA v4.1)
- dropped: 0067 (fbdev deferred-I/O flush, upstream fbdev rework; only the RAM shell used it)
- duo.config: CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_IRIS off so venus keeps the SM8150 compatible
